---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { DocsTable } from '@/molecules/DocComponents/DocComponents';

const ROLES = [
  ['Coder', 'Build and execute isolated workspaces; report build and agent state'],
  ['OpenFlows Manager', 'Authorize users and runtimes; broker GitHub credentials; provision workspaces through Coder'],
  ['Nexus', "Coordinate one tenant's issue-to-PR flow, worker assignments, hooks, and A2A evidence"],
];
---

<DocsLayout breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' }, { label: 'Concepts', href: '/docs/concepts' }, { label: 'The Coder / OpenFlows Split' }]}>
  <h1>The Coder / OpenFlows split</h1>
  <p>Coder decides where agents execute. Manager decides which user and tenant may run a workspace, which template and repository it uses, and what scoped credentials it may receive. Nexus decides how agents collaborate on that tenant's work.</p>
  <DocsTable headers={['Component', 'Primary responsibility']} rows={ROLES} />
  <p>The Manager holds the platform Coder operator credential and GitHub App private key. Nexus and workers register as workspace runtimes and receive only their own tenant-scoped bundle and short-lived credentials. Manager asks Coder to perform workspace lifecycle operations on their behalf.</p>
  <p>Read <a href="/docs/architecture/manager-runtime">Manager Runtime</a> and <a href="/docs/architecture/credentials">Credentials and Trust</a> for the protocol and security boundaries.</p>
</DocsLayout>
